{"name":"Sea Cliff","hex":"#a5c7df","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sea Cliff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sea_Cliff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cliffed coast","blocks":[{"text":"A cliffed coast, also called an abrasion coast, is a form of coast where the action of marine waves has formed steep cliffs that may or may not be precipitous. It contrasts with a flat or alluvial coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cliffed_coast_%28shematic_view%29.svg/330px-Cliffed_coast_%28shematic_view%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliffed_coast"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/500px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/1280px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG/500px-Klippenk%C3%BCste.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crags on the southwestern coast of